# Runtime data
#
# backend/data/ holds the curated corpus: statutory text, patent and
# multi-omics notes, the blueprint workbook, and the committed snapshot of
# official external datasets. That is content, not runtime state, and it must be
# versioned - the corpus manifest hashes it and detects drift between
# deployments, which is impossible if a fresh clone ships an empty corpus.
# Only the incremental harvester state and local stores stay ignored.
!backend/data/
backend/data/*_state.json
backend/data/knowledge_graph.json
backend/data/uploads/
backend/data/exports/
backend/uploads/
backend/exports/
backend/*.db
backend/*.sqlite3
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Local indices / stores (rebuilt at runtime)
backend/app/rag/faiss_index/
backend/app/rag/qdrant_local_data/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Model caches / downloaded models
*.hf_cache/
.huggingface/

# Logs
*.log

